text:
anna: quick heads-up — opened a PR to consolidate the structured-output and tool-invocation snippets for the migration guide: https://github.com/redwood-inference/docs/pull/452

mike: thanks anna. skimmed — big picture looks solid. a couple of questions: do we preserve the old `function_call` examples or replace them entirely?

sam: i'd replace most of the examples but keep a short compatibility note. users still reference `function_call` in older SDKs.

jorge: agreed. also found one doc that assumes the runtime returns `tool_name` instead of `tool`. PR should normalize to `tool` across examples.

anna: good catch. sam — can you swap the examples where we show client code + schema? i'll drop a template below for the new shape.

sam: yep. putting a minimal example here so reviewers can copy-paste:```json
{
  "type": "object",
  "properties": {
    "tool": {"type": "string"},
    "args": {"type": "object"},
    "confidence": {"type": "number"}
  },
  "required": ["tool", "args"]
}
```

mike: nit: can we make `args` allow both object and array? some tools accept positional args. maybe: `{"oneOf":[{"type":"object"},{"type":"array"}]}`

jorge: +1 on the oneOf. also add a short JSON schema example for a common tool (url_fetch) so docs show concrete usage. e.g.```json
{
  "type":"object",
  "properties":{
    "tool":{"type":"string","enum":["url_fetch","lookup_db"]},
    "args":{
      "oneOf":[
        {"type":"object","properties":{"url":{"type":"string"}},"required":["url"]},
        {"type":"array"}
      ]
    }
  },
  "required":["tool","args"]
}
```

anna: perfect. i'll update the PR with that schema and a short migration note: "If you previously relied on `function_call.name`, map to `tool` and move params under `args`."

sam: also add a short parsing pattern for SDKs: example JS snippet:```js
const resp = await client.generate(...);
const parsed = JSON.parse(resp);
const {tool, args} = parsed;
if (tool === 'url_fetch') { await fetch(args.url); }
```

mike: can we add a warning about trusting `confidence` blindly? maybe say: "confidence is model-provided and should be validated against domain heuristics".

anna: good call. i'll add a short callout and link to the evals page.

devex-bot: CI: docs linting passed for PR #452 — 3 files changed, 12 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-) (check: https://ci.internal/redwood/452) :white_check_mark:

jorge: our internal snippet-checker flagged one broken link in the migration guide (old sdk reference). i'll paste the failing line: `See /sdk/python/old-tooling`

sam: i'll replace with `/sdk/python/migration#tool-calls`.

mike: do we need a retroactive redirect for the old path? marketing will choke if external links 404.

anna: i'll open a separate tiny PR to add a redirect YAML to `_redirects` — will tag marketing.

sam: who wants to do final review after you push updates? i can if no one else is free.

anna: appreciate it — please do sam. i'll ping when ready.

mike: quick checklist before merge: update examples (done), add compatibility note (todo), add oneOf for args (todo), warning about confidence (todo), fix links (todo), add redirect PR (separate).

anna: checklist noted. target to land by EOD tomorrow. thanks all :rocket:
